        <body>
            <div xml:id="d111-a3">

                <pb facs="d111-4" n="4" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v03mSupp/d111-4"/>


                <head>Note from Carson to John Foster
                    Dulles</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1958-11-29">November 29,
                        1958</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d111-5" n="5" type="facsimile" xml:id="d111-5"/>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Basic National Policy</hi></p>
                <p>In approving the attached memo from Mr. Smith, Mr. Dillon indicated that he thought it unwise for you to mention
                    the specific example of a national sales tax, since this is a controversial form
                    of taxation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">James Carson</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Duty Officer</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
